# Dog Park, https://dogpark.lynrummy.com (DEPLOY.md, step 8). Installed on
# prod as /etc/caddy/sites/dogpark.lynrummy.com.caddy, which angry-gopher's
# deploy/Caddyfile imports beside lynrummy.com's site block. Caddy holds the
# certificate and HTTPS; Dog Park's droplet listens only on its private card.
#
# <dogpark-private-address> is the droplet's private address (DEPLOY.md, step
# 6). It is not an address, so left in, Caddy should refuse the file
# (not tried: the box has no Caddy).
#
# The body cap is the app's own, 64 KiB (src/play/physics_server.zig's
# most_body), with room: the app refuses past it either way. The headers are
# lynrummy.com's.
dogpark.lynrummy.com {
	encode gzip
	request_body {
		max_size 1MiB
	}
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN"
	}
	# Every request, as Caddy saw it (Steve, 2026-10-16: the droplet's own
	# request list keeps only the newest few, so who knocked was lost), to
	# /var/log/caddy/dogpark-access.log: angry-gopher's deploy/Caddyfile
	# defines `access_log` for every site on prod (metal-vmm QUEUE 221).
	import access_log dogpark
	reverse_proxy <dogpark-private-address>:80
}
